until none is. Then dummies whose \eqn{|t|} has fallen below \code{cval} are
removed one at a time, and forward and backward passes alternate until
nothing changes.

With \code{method = "isat"}, the search is impulse and step indicator
saturation by \code{\link[gets:isat]{gets::isat()}} (Hendry, Johansen and Santos, 2008; Castle,
Doornik, Hendry and Pretis, 2015), with the regressors of the ADL kept and
the indicators selected at the significance level that corresponds to
\code{cval} (two-sided normal). It needs the \code{gets} package. \code{isat()} chooses
among its terminal models by an information criterion, so it can keep a
dummy whose \eqn{|t|} is slightly below \code{cval}.

\strong{Breaks in x.} To find the dates for \code{\link[=super_exogeneity_test]{super_exogeneity_test()}}, run
